 "method": "Library-level: FileInfo::run on each input with the registered or oracle flags; text and TSV compared byte for byte with the oracle files after replacing the 'File name: ' text line and the 'general: file name' TSV line, which embed the path; retained outputs compared with FuzzyDiff as registered.",
 "evidence_tier": 1,
 "evidence": "Tier 1 (executed differential): the product-SDK FileInfo tool (Debug, core 4fdec46; installed FileInfo.h and FileHandler.h equal to the pin; the C1 manifest records no output-relevant change on the traced call path) wrote the text and TSV reports of 31 runs: 7 from C1 (../oracle/topp-early-bundle run1: FileInfo_1/2/3/9 with -out_tsv, empty featureXML, empty mzML, retained FeatureFinderCentroided_1 output) and 24 from this package (../oracle/file-info-core, two runs reproduced byte for byte). All 31 text and 31 TSV reports equal the Rust reports except where a known mzML reader gap outside this package refuses the input (FileInfo_9, empty.mzML, FileInfo_12) or loads it differently (MzMLFile_1, selected-ion drift time); those 5 tests are ignored with the reason and guarded by a tripwire, and three derived inputs whose C++ reports equal the originals apart from the file name are compared instead. Tier 1 (retained upstream output): TOPP_FileInfo_1, _2, _3 and _9 pass FuzzyDiff as registered (FileInfo_9 on the derived input). Tier 3: seven of the nine FileInfo_test.cpp sections transcribed; consensusXML and FASTA pending for A7 with the explicit refusal asserted. Tier 4: refusals, error classes, defaults, structured-result consistency. None of the reports holds a default-stream tie of the Apple libc class, and no case exits non-zero, so no Debug-only precondition is involved.",
 "native_implementation": [
  "src/format/file_info/model.rs",
  "src/format/file_info/report.rs",
  "src/format/file_info/peaks.rs",
  "src/format/file_info/features.rs"
 ],
 "native_tests": [
